---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'location', text: 'Config location', level: 2 },
  { id: 'options', text: 'Options', level: 2 },
  { id: 'privacy', text: 'Privacy', level: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Settings" headings={headings}>
  <h2 id="location">Config location</h2>
  <p>MarkRust uses the operating system’s configuration directory:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> typically <code>~/Library/Application Support/markrust/config.toml</code></li>
    <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/markrust/config.toml</code> (usually <code>~/.config/markrust/config.toml</code>)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="options">Options</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`theme = "dark"          # "dark" or "light"\nfont_family = "Inter"\nfont_size = 16\ncode_font_family = "Menlo"\nautosave_ms = 1000    # debounce in milliseconds`} lang="toml" filename="config.toml" />

  <p>Recent workspaces are stored beside the settings as <code>recent.json</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>MarkRust collects no telemetry and has no analytics, account system, or automatic crash-report upload. If the app panics, it writes a local diagnostic log; configuration and recent-workspace data stay on your machine.</p>
</DocsLayout>
